Subject: [PATCH 49/90] Far terrain draws snow: snow layers of saved chunks and
 the climate's snow on generated far land

A snow layer is thin and not kept in far columns, so the grass under it showed and far snowy plains and peaks came out green. Saved chunks' columns now draw a snow layer as the snow block's top on the ground under it (Column::from_chunk, with its test), and land sampled straight from the generator (no decoration) gets the snow block's top where freeze_top_layer would lay snow: the biome has precipitation and is cold enough at that height (FarSnow).

UMP: snowy plains seen from 140 high, far band white share 0.02 -> 0.26 (ump/scripts/snow_check.ps1).
